<title>USA: University of Ark. deal yields 5.35 pct in 2009.</title>
<headline>University of Ark. deal yields 5.35 pct in 2009.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Llama Co said Thursday it tentatively priced $12.3 million Board of Trustees of the University of Arkansas refunding revenue bonds at a top yield of 5.35 percent in 2009.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:  </p>
<p>BOARD OF TRUSTEES OF THE UNIVERSITY OF</p>
<p>ARKANSAS VARIOUS REFUNDING REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>(FAYETTEVILE CAMPUS)</p>
<p>RE: $12,300,000*</p>
<p>SERIES 1996</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: A1		    S&amp;P: NA</p>
<p>		 (EXPECTED)</p>
<p>    DATED: 11/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 05/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 11/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	  PRICE</p>
<p>11/01/1997		1,535M    3.90  %	100.00</p>
<p>11/01/1998		1,355M    4.15  %	100.00</p>
<p>11/01/1999		1,415M    4.30  %	100.00</p>
<p>11/01/2000		1,475M    4.45  %	100.00</p>
<p>11/01/2001		1,540M    4.55  %	100.00</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>11/01/2002		1,610M    4.65  %	100.00</p>
